# AoC 2022 Day 5 Part 1 — the full crate simulation ("CMZ").
#
# The drawing parses column-wise: Ragged Columns transposes the unpadded
# lines, the crate letters of stack k live in column 4(k-1)+1, and the
# Filter drops the blanks and the stack label. list() packs the three
# stacks (top first); Fold From: moves threads them through every move —
# set/item/take/drop/reverse/concat do the crate surgery — and the tops
# join into the answer.
Cursed Energy: input.txt
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n\n"

Channel "s1":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 0
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Cursed Technique: Ragged Columns
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 1
    Cursed Technique: Filter
        Using: (ch) -> occurrences("0123456789 ", ch) = 0

Channel "s2":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 0
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Cursed Technique: Ragged Columns
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 5
    Cursed Technique: Filter
        Using: (ch) -> occurrences("0123456789 ", ch) = 0

Channel "s3":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 0
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Cursed Technique: Ragged Columns
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 9
    Cursed Technique: Filter
        Using: (ch) -> occurrences("0123456789 ", ch) = 0

Channel "moves":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 1
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Cursed Technique: Match Pattern
        Using: "move {n:int} from {f:int} to {t:int}"

Maximum Technique: Combine
    From: s1, s2, s3
    Using: (a, b, c) -> list(a, b, c)

Maximum Technique: Fold
    From: moves
    Using: (st, m) -> set(set(st, m.t - 1, concat(reverse(take(item(st, m.f - 1), m.n)), item(st, m.t - 1))), m.f - 1, drop(item(st, m.f - 1), m.n))

Cursed Technique: Map Each
    Using: (s) -> first(s)

Maximum Technique: Join
Reveal: stdout
